{
	title: 'Thinking signatures live in blobs',
	spec: 'Thinking signatures are stored as session text blobs (host/blobs.ts, sessions/<id>/blobs/), not inline in history.asonl: the thinking block holds the blob id instead of the signature, and providers read the signature back when they build a request, as they do image blobs. Provider replay is unchanged: the same signatures reach the same provider. Histories written before this keep their inline signatures and still replay; there is no migration. Measured before the change: signatures were 31% of one 153 kB session history (25 signatures, 47.7 kB, the largest 3.3 kB).',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'history.blockRecord writes a signed thinking block with signatureBlob (a .txt blob via blobs.storeOutput) instead of signature; history.messages puts the signature back and drops signatureBlob, so providers get the block as streamed. The live turn keeps its in-memory signature. Forks copy the blob directory, so references survive. A missing blob throws (corrupt history), per the fail-fast rule.'
	],
	needs: ['bz']
}
